{{also|из}}
==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ru|изо-}} {{i|before certain consonant clusters}}
* {{l|ru|ис-}} {{i|before voiceless consonants}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|из-|ann=y}}
* {{ru-IPA|и́з-|ann=y}} {{i|when stressed}}

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*jьz-}}; see {{m|sla-pro|*jьz}} for further information.

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|cat2=verbal prefixes}}

# [[out]] [[from]]
#: {{m|ru|[[идти́]]|to go}} → {{m|ru|[[исходить|изойти́]]|to emanate, to originate, to come from}}
# {{n-g|When added to a verb, it may form a verb with a sense of completeness, abundance or exhaustion.}}
#: {{m|ru|[[укра́сить]]|to decorate}} → {{m|ru|[[изукра́сить]]|lavishly decorate}}
# {{n-g|When added to a verb, it may form a verb with a sense of destruction, ruined due to use.}}
#: {{m|ru|[[писа́ть]]|to write}} → {{m|ru|[[исписа́ть]]|write upon, cover with notes, write over}}
# {{n-g|When added to nouns, especially when they have the suffix -ье, it indicates location of an object.}}
#: {{m|ru|[[голова́]]|head}} → {{m|ru|[[изголо́вье]]|head of the bed}}
# {{n-g|When added to adjectives for colours, an adverb is formed indicating nuance.}}
#: {{m|ru|[[жёлтый]]|yellow}} → {{m|ru|[[изжелта-|и́зжелта-бу́рый]]|yellowish-brown}}
# {{n-g|When added to adjectives, it may form an adverb indicating spatial or temporal properties. Usually in archaic or highly formal style.}}
#: {{m|ru|[[да́льний]]|far, distant}} → {{m|ru|[[и́здали]]|from afar}}
# {{n-g|When added to adverbs, it can form an adverb with a sense of direction for an action.}}
#: {{m|ru|[[вну́тренний]]|interior, inner}} → {{m|ru|[[изнутри́]]|from within, from inside}}

